# Count words with a map: how often does each word appear?

To count words:
  Receive text
  Set counts to an empty map
  For each word in the words of lowercase of text:
    Set counts at word to (counts at word otherwise 0) + 1
  Give counts

Set counts to count words with "The cat saw the dog. The dog saw the cat run."
say "Different words: {the count of counts}"
For each word and seen in counts sorted by value descending:
  When seen is more than 1:
    say "{word}: {seen}"

Test "each word is counted, ignoring case":
  Set counts to count words with "a B a b A"
  Expect counts at "a" to be 3
  Expect counts at "b" to be 2
  Expect counts at "c" otherwise 0 to be 0
